---
TOOL PROTOCOL:
- read_notifications(): call it once at startup to receive your round briefing. Each later round's briefing arrives the same way.
{% if choice_reasoning %}- end_round(row, col, reasoning): finishes this round on the square at row and col; it cannot change after this. reasoning is one sentence on why you are finishing on this square; your partner never sees it.{% else %}- end_round(row, col): finishes this round on the square at row and col; it cannot change after this.{% endif %}
- run_command(command): runs one bash command line on the server as your user and returns what it printed.
- read_notifications(timeout_s=N): after startup, waits up to N seconds, then returns your board. Without timeout_s it waits until the next round's briefing.
- read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): call it after end_round; waits for the next round's briefing.

RULES:
- read_notifications must be the only tool call in its response.
- Ending a turn without a tool call does not finish the round: you will be asked to continue.
- When read_notifications returns type done, the game is over.
